# hda: the Intel HD Audio driver (drivers/hda), as devmgr binds it to the
# board's HD Audio controller. Served on the driver's DR_SERVE channel; the
# shell's `hda` command is the client.
# Format: see tools/genidl.py.
#
# The driver reads the controller and every codec's widget graph, picks
# the path from a DAC to the headphones and sets it up muted, with the
# pin's output off: it makes no sound yet. The playback methods come with
# the rest of the audio work (docs/A1-PLAN.md).
#
# Reconnect (devmgr's supervision, user/include/devmgr.h): a call that
# fails with ERR_PEER_CLOSED means the driver died; get the channel from
# devmgr again (DEVMGR_GET_SERVICE) and retry. The driver keeps nothing
# across a restart.

protocol hda 21

# The dump, read from the codecs now: the same lines the driver printed
# to the kernel log at start, as text in a new VMO of `length` bytes
# (lines end in \n). codecs: how many codecs answered.
1  dump  ()  -> (handle text, u32 length, u32 codecs)

# What the driver chose and set up. codec, pin, dac: the path's codec
# address and its two ends (pin 0: there is no path, and the rest is 0).
# pcm and formats: the DAC's Supported PCM Size/Rates and Stream Formats
# parameters (spec 7.3: 20:16 sample sizes, 11:0 rates). amp: its output
# amplifier's capabilities (bit 31 mute, 22:16 step size in quarter dB
# minus 1, 14:8 steps, 6:0 the step that is 0 dB; 0: it has none). jack:
# 0 unknown (jack detection is not built yet). nodes: the path's node ids
# from the DAC to the pin, `count` of them. text: what is set on each
# node, read back from the codec, as one line (NUL-terminated).
2  info  ()  -> (u32 codec, u32 pin, u32 dac, u32 pcm, u32 formats, u32 amp, u32 jack, u32 count, u8[8] nodes, u8[240] text)
